00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.568
-Our next guest is an
Emmy-nominated writer, comedian,

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:04.004
and actor you know from his work
on "Saturday Night Live."

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:07.474
He stars in the scripted podcast
"Hot White Heist,"

00:00:07.474 --> 00:00:09.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is available exclusively
through Audible.

00:00:09.909 --> 00:00:13.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
Please welcome back to the sho
our friend Bowen Yang.

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:14.948 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
How are you, Bowen?

00:00:14.948 --> 00:00:17.684 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Hi, Seth. I'm good.

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:20.520 size:81% position:41%
What an honor to be in
this Denverite show,

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:23.256 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, just to share the bill
with Peyton.

00:00:23.256 --> 00:00:24.691 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's right.

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:25.492 line:92%
You spent time in Colorado

00:00:25.492 --> 00:00:26.659 align:start size:94% position:6%
and of course, Peyton Mannin
lives there now.

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:30.296
I did not realize how Rock
Mountain high tonight was.

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:32.699 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I get altitude sickness
whenever I go back,

00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:35.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I've lost my powers.
-Did you really?

00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:37.303 align:start size:94% position:6%
You've just been gone
for a little amount of time,

00:00:37.303 --> 00:00:38.438 size:81% position:41% line:92%
and you can't go back?

00:00:38.438 --> 00:00:39.172 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-I can't go back, no.

00:00:39.172 --> 00:00:41.708
-Wow, and that probably explains
why you're in Georgia now.

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:44.978 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Exactly, I'm in Georgia.
I'm fulfilling my uncle duties

00:00:44.978 --> 00:00:47.781 align:start size:94% position:6%
in Georgia for the first tim
since the pandemic.

00:00:47.781 --> 00:00:48.415 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's wonderful.

00:00:48.415 --> 00:00:51.217
-Do you have nieces and nephews,
one of each?

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:52.152 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
What do you got?

00:00:52.152 --> 00:00:53.520 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I got two nieces.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:54.854 size:84% position:42% line:92%
The older one is three.

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:58.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's just starting to tal
and express herself

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:02.929 align:start size:94% position:6%
and set her own boundaries
or defy others.

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:05.498 size:78% position:39% line:92%
And it's interesting.

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:08.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
Right now, we're teaching he
how to cough properly.

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:10.136 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, got you.
-Just to cover your mouth.

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:15.608
It's really -- It's really
strange to do it in public

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:17.911 align:start size:94% position:6%
to teach a child how to coug
properly in public.

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:20.413 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I'm doing more than the CD
is in terms of,

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:23.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, knowing how to do --
-Yeah.

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:25.251 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I wouldn't call yo
a first responder,

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:28.688 size:78% position:39%
but it does seem like
you're responsive.

00:01:28.688 --> 00:01:29.789 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-There you go.

00:01:29.789 --> 00:01:31.991 line:92%
Tertiary responder? Happy to be.

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:35.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Are you good with kids
historically?

00:01:35.195 --> 00:01:41.201 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No. In fact, I think this i
just kind of confirming

00:01:41.201 --> 00:01:44.904 align:start size:94% position:6%
for myself that I'm terrible
with kids.

00:01:44.904 --> 00:01:49.008
The older niece is getting upset
and she's crying sometimes

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:50.210 align:start size:94% position:6%
then I'll just turn around
and go,

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:53.713
"Ellie, I'm not seeing any
tears," like an acting coach

00:01:53.713 --> 00:01:55.815 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Like, I'm awful.

00:01:55.815 --> 00:02:00.286
And then the other day, she wa
drinking water out of a cup.

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:02.188 line:92%
She refused to have ice in it.

00:02:02.188 --> 00:02:05.258 align:start size:94% position:6%
She loves Elsa from "Frozen,
however.

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:06.759 line:92%
And I said to her, I said,

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:09.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Ellie, you know who loves ice
is Elsa.

00:02:09.329 --> 00:02:11.764 align:start size:94% position:6%
And if you love Elsa,
shouldn't you love ice?"

00:02:11.764 --> 00:02:14.634 line:92%
And she -- Her eyes glazed ove

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:17.237
and I think I throttled he
into an existential crisis

00:02:17.237 --> 00:02:19.539 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
So I'm terrible with kids.

00:02:19.539 --> 00:02:22.842 size:81% position:41%
-Well, you're good at
a lot of other things,

00:02:22.842 --> 00:02:24.978 size:84% position:42% line:92%
including this podcast.

00:02:24.978 --> 00:02:27.647 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is a "Heist" Audible
podcast.

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:29.282 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-It's an all-queer cast.

00:02:29.282 --> 00:02:30.917 line:92%
And I want you to explain it

00:02:30.917 --> 00:02:31.985 line:92%
You were on the "Today" show

00:02:31.985 --> 00:02:32.986 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they asked you
to explain it.

00:02:32.986 --> 00:02:35.388 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then they told you to
remember it was a morning show

00:02:35.388 --> 00:02:39.225 align:start size:94% position:6%
Look, it's a different sid
of morning right now.

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:40.960 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're on the other side
of midnight.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:43.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
Go wild.
Explain it how you wish.

00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:46.933 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What I couldn't say to
Jenna Bush Hager was that it i

00:02:46.933 --> 00:02:52.338
an Audible-scripted podcas
about a sperm-bank heist

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:55.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
in which we were stealing
the sperm

00:02:55.542 --> 00:02:58.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
of all of our past president
since Kennedy

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:02.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the sperm of
Yo-Yo Ma, Mark Zuckerberg,

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:03.816 line:92%
the guy who invented the Segway.

00:03:03.816 --> 00:03:07.587 align:start size:94% position:6%
Our greatest minds
have their sperm stored

00:03:07.587 --> 00:03:08.321 size:81% position:41% line:92%
under the Space Needle

00:03:08.321 --> 00:03:10.690 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we have to pull off
an all-queer heist

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:16.596
in order to serve a group of
lesbian militants in Montana

00:03:16.596 --> 00:03:18.865 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-That's the pitch.

00:03:18.865 --> 00:03:19.632 line:92%
-That's a very good pitch.

00:03:19.632 --> 00:03:21.401
And I feel like people could'v
handled that in the morning.

00:03:21.401 --> 00:03:23.469
I got to be honest.
I think that that would be fine.

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:25.905 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Yeah, I think so too.

00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:31.077
-I want to ask. You play
a sort of grifter of sorts

00:03:31.077 --> 00:03:33.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
You came to New York
to go to NYU.

00:03:33.079 --> 00:03:38.785
Were you one of those sort o
clear-eyed maybe, sort of mayb

00:03:38.785 --> 00:03:40.820
overtrusting people when
you first got to New York?

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:45.258 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Absolutely. I was swindled ou
of my entire net worth

00:03:45.258 --> 00:03:47.093 align:start size:94% position:6%
within two months
of moving here.

00:03:47.093 --> 00:03:51.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was Halloween 2008,
a week before the election

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:55.668 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I decided to walk over
to the parade.

00:03:55.668 --> 00:03:59.305 align:start size:94% position:6%
Or no, I was walking
to some dorm,

00:03:59.305 --> 00:04:02.442 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I crossed the street
at Union Square.

00:04:02.442 --> 00:04:03.843 line:92%
And someone stopped me and said,

00:04:03.843 --> 00:04:06.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Hey, you stepped on
my glasses"

00:04:06.079 --> 00:04:08.114 size:78% position:39%
and held up this pair
of shattered frames,

00:04:08.114 --> 00:04:09.249 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he was like,
"I need these to see.

00:04:09.249 --> 00:04:12.385 align:start size:94% position:6%
You need to pay me $100
right now."

00:04:12.385 --> 00:04:14.387 size:84% position:42% line:92%
I said, "I am so sorry.

00:04:14.387 --> 00:04:15.722 line:92%
I don't believe I did that

00:04:15.722 --> 00:04:19.692 align:start size:94% position:6%
but if I did,
I don't have the money."

00:04:19.692 --> 00:04:23.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
He kept following me,
and then I had gotten --

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:24.597 line:92%
I had acquiesced at that point

00:04:24.597 --> 00:04:26.866 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was just like, "Fine, you ca
come with me to the ATM.

00:04:26.866 --> 00:04:29.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
I need to pick up some cash,
but I have to tell you,

00:04:29.636 --> 00:04:31.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have $13 in my bank accoun
right now,

00:04:31.437 --> 00:04:34.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I do need to call my father
so he could deposit

00:04:34.073 --> 00:04:37.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
at least $7 for me
to give you $20."

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:44.550
And so then, his face fell and
he was like, "Oh, okay, sure."

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:46.219
And I think he felt sorry for me
at that point,

00:04:46.219 --> 00:04:49.188
so that when we were waiting for
the money to transfer

00:04:49.188 --> 00:04:53.660
at the ATM, he's making really
really polite small talk with me

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:56.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
and being like, "You know,
there's this parade every year

00:04:56.663 --> 00:04:57.430 line:92%
and it's really wonderful.

00:04:57.430 --> 00:05:00.133 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, you just moved to New York
You'd love this parade."

00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:01.934 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was being very kind to me
afterward.

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:03.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's very nice. He realized
you were going to be out

00:05:03.703 --> 00:05:07.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
20 bucks but he didn't wan
your whole night to be a wash.

00:05:07.073 --> 00:05:08.207 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Exactly.

00:05:08.207 --> 00:05:11.811
-You had such a wonderful season
on "SNL."

00:05:11.811 --> 00:05:12.378 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Congratulations.

00:05:12.378 --> 00:05:16.416
I think the thing that
I would've least predicted maybe

00:05:16.416 --> 00:05:19.552
going into the season is tha
you would play Fran Lebowitz

00:05:19.552 --> 00:05:25.358
I think that I may be equall
enamored with Fran to you.

00:05:25.358 --> 00:05:26.726 line:92%
How did this even come about

00:05:26.726 --> 00:05:30.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because it's not, let's say,
natural casting.

00:05:30.096 --> 00:05:31.564 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-No, it's not.

00:05:31.564 --> 00:05:33.900 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I kind of wanted to go
for it anyway.

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:38.271
I was just, let's say, under the
influence of something in be

00:05:38.271 --> 00:05:39.772 line:92%
watching "Pretend It's a City.

00:05:39.772 --> 00:05:42.642 size:88% position:44%
And I thought to myself,
"I'm going to play her.

00:05:42.642 --> 00:05:43.876 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm going to play her
on 'Update.'"

00:05:43.876 --> 00:05:46.179 size:88% position:44%
And then I texted one of
the writers, Sudi Green,

00:05:46.179 --> 00:05:48.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
a very good friend and I said,
"I have this crazy idea,

00:05:48.681 --> 00:05:51.617
but I think I have to play
Fran Lebowitz on 'Update.'

00:05:51.617 --> 00:05:53.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then she said,
"That's great.

00:05:53.286 --> 00:05:55.288 line:92%
Let's get Kyle as Scorsese."

00:05:55.288 --> 00:05:56.122 size:81% position:41% line:92%
I was like, "Perfect."

00:05:56.122 --> 00:05:58.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, the next day,
Anna Drezen, our head writer

00:05:58.591 --> 00:06:01.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
texted me, "Crazy idea,
but I think you should pla

00:06:01.594 --> 00:06:02.428 line:92%
Fran Lebowitz on 'Update.'

00:06:02.428 --> 00:06:04.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said, "Sudi and I had
the same thought."

00:06:04.697 --> 00:06:07.800 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then we did it
the Saturday afterwards.

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:10.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like, this is
the best part of working here,

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:14.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that you get to ideate
something so silly

00:06:14.674 --> 00:06:17.510
the week before and then have it
be on TV the next week.

00:06:17.510 --> 00:06:21.414
-Everyone I talked to loved it
and yet, there was one person,

00:06:21.414 --> 00:06:24.283 size:88% position:44%
a sort of notable person
who did not care for it

00:06:24.283 --> 00:06:26.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
and recently went on the recor
as not caring for it.

00:06:26.452 --> 00:06:30.490 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's right.
Fran herself has gone from -

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:32.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
Andy Cohen had
reached out for comment.

00:06:32.525 --> 00:06:35.995
She had said that she has
no interest in seeing it,

00:06:35.995 --> 00:06:37.430 line:92%
which I loved at the time.

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:40.933 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I think last week
she's gone on record

00:06:40.933 --> 00:06:43.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
to say that
she does not like it.

00:06:43.403 --> 00:06:47.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I think that's
confirmation that she's seen i

00:06:47.073 --> 00:06:48.508 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that she doesn't
care for it.

00:06:48.508 --> 00:06:51.844
And I think that's the highest
compliment you can possibly ge

00:06:51.844 --> 00:06:54.247 size:84% position:42%
from someone like Fran.
-I think that's right.

00:06:54.247 --> 00:06:56.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think that
if Fran Lebowitz said,

00:06:56.182 --> 00:06:59.952
"Oh, my God, I loved it, and
it's so cool to be on 'SNL,'

00:06:59.952 --> 00:07:01.788 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, it would just
ruin everything.

00:07:01.788 --> 00:07:03.623 line:92%
-Terrible, yeah, absolutely.

00:07:03.623 --> 00:07:05.458 line:92%
So I wear it as a badge of honor

00:07:05.458 --> 00:07:08.528 size:78% position:39%
that she did not like
my portrayal of her.

00:07:08.528 --> 00:07:09.762 line:92%
I probably wouldn't either

00:07:09.762 --> 00:07:14.567
If, like, someone who is like so
demographically opposite of me

00:07:14.567 --> 00:07:17.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
portrayed me, I'd be like,
"Come on." So no.

00:07:17.437 --> 00:07:19.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I bet even if you were
demographically

00:07:19.472 --> 00:07:22.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
right on the nose, she probabl
would've felt the same way

00:07:22.041 --> 00:07:23.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
Okay, fair, fair.

00:07:23.543 --> 00:07:24.577 line:92%
-I mean, she's Fran Lebowitz

00:07:24.577 --> 00:07:30.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
We'll give her a lot of spac
to be critical of things.

00:07:30.082 --> 00:07:31.484 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Sure. Absolutely.

00:07:31.484 --> 00:07:34.520 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hey, thanks so much
for being here.

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:35.721 align:start size:94% position:6%
Congrats again on
another great year.

00:07:35.721 --> 00:07:38.658
And congrats on the podcast.
Thanks for being here, Bowen

00:07:38.658 --> 00:07:39.926 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Thanks, Seth.

00:07:39.926 --> 00:07:42.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Hot White Heist" --
here it is --

00:07:42.161 --> 00:07:44.997 align:start size:94% position:6%
is available exclusively
through Audible.

